    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1293">

                <pb facs="0884" n="768" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg768"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.115/41.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to Vice Consul
                        Guyant.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-01-09">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 9, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your January 8th. Make urgent protest against any attempt to exact forced loans
                    from foreigners. If, however, authorities persist in attempt, advise foreigners
                    to pay under protest, making protest a matter of record if possible, and to
                    secure receipts.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moore</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
